en:
That they were killed by Hanako-san is a lie.
What really happened was much crueler.
I'll tell you that story.{p}

She was locked in the girls' restroom on the third floor of the old school building.
In the second stall from the back of the girls' restroom.
Then they wedged a bar against the door from outside so she couldn't get out.{p}

...So this old school building will be torn down in just a few more days.
The old building held no particular nostalgia for me, yet it filled me with a strange melancholy.
I fell under the illusion that I had known it ever since it was brand new, freshly built.{p}

I took another look at the old school building.
For some reason, I found myself praying that it would never vanish.
If this is a dream, may I never wake from it...{p}

Suddenly my body seemed to float into the air, and then I was slammed into the ceiling with tremendous force.
I was completely upside down, as if gravity were coming from the ceiling.
I must have hit my back hard when I was slammed into it.{p}

I saw it clearly.
The masked woman had taken off her mask and was looking up at me.
With a face shining like an angel's...{p}

And then she said,
"Seven... Seven, is it?
Were you really listening to what you were told? Liar..."{p}

I listened to her in silence.
I understood that they were victims.
But driving so many people to their deaths to drag them along... I wasn't so sure about that...{p}

Just then, a single ray of morning sun shone in.
The light fell on her face...
And then, for an instant, her face stirred and rippled.{p}

The clatter of the mask hitting the floor brought me back to my senses.
When the mask wobbled and fell, she was already gone.
She had vanished along with the butterflies.{p}

Had I seen an illusion, or had I been dreaming...?
Then I noticed a single butterfly fluttering around me, as if reluctant to leave.
The morning sun had already fully risen.{p}

"Uh, waaaaaaaaah☆"
My voice rang out through the old school building.
When my voice, echoing through the building, finally died away, a silence that seemed eternal returned.{p}

She looked up and gazed all around the sky.
As if she were someone who had forgotten to look at the sky for years...
I couldn't see her face behind the mask, but that was how it felt to me.{p}

...At that moment.
Her face suddenly began to crumble.
Like wax running in the heat, her face melted and flowed away.{p}

That's right.
There's no way I can be saved.
But you know, I'm not all alone anymore...{p}

"Iwashita, please..."
Had I lost my mind?
Answering a question like that.{p}

Iwashita... the one who had once tried to kill me.
Maybe I felt guilty toward Uchiyama.
Maybe that was why I chose Iwashita.{p}

You're an indecisive person, aren't you.
...Well, fine.
There's no need to go out of my way to show it to someone who doesn't want to see it.{p}

...Now, try to save me.
Me, back when I was being bullied...
With that, she put the mask on me.{p}

"Thank you. Thank you, {a}."
Somewhere far off, I heard a voice thanking me.
I turned around to look...{p}

I was in the restroom of the real old school building.
There was no one there anymore.
Not even the six...{p}

A dazzling flash of light shot through the room.
That was when it happened.
They vanished like smoke.{p}

'Cause I've gone and fallen for you, {a}.
...Just kidding!
But the part about coming to get you is true. Look forward to it."{p}

The slanting sunlight pierced my eyes fiercely.
I'll go home and sleep.
And just for today, I'll skip school.{p}

I chose Fukuzawa.
Fukuzawa was a first-year, just like me.
I felt bad for Iwashita, but I felt closer to Fukuzawa.{p}

"............"
Her face looked terribly sad.
All I could do was silently look into her deep, sorrowful eyes.{p}

I ran at full speed.
"I must have... put a good distance... between us by now..."
I looked back.{p}

"Whoa!"
He was still following me☆
About fifty meters behind, same as before, with a terrifying look on his face.{p}

I ran with everything I had.
My heart felt like it was about to burst.
"It's no use... I can't... run any farther..."{p}

My heart was screaming.
It felt like even the slightest jolt would make it burst.
Everything before my eyes was going blurry...{p}

"By Fukuzawa..."
I picked Fukuzawa.
Surely Fukuzawa wouldn't kill me in some horrible way.{p}

(That's my leg... My leg, which was moving just a moment ago...)
Saying, "Here you go, enjoy," Fukuzawa brought the meat to my mouth.
The thought of being made to eat that meat sickened me so much I almost forgot the pain in my leg.{p}

"Come on, we're treating you to a nice meal here. Hurry up and eat."
With that, Shindo forced my mouth open.
The fresh meat, cut away only a moment ago, was shoved into my mouth.{p}

"Come on, there's plenty more, so don't be shy."
Fukuzawa kept pushing more and more into my mouth.
I couldn't take it anymore and spewed up everything in my stomach.{p}

"Ewwwww, gross!
You can't do that! It's wrong to waste food."
Fukuzawa scooped up the spewed-out mess with her hands and poured it into my mouth.{p}

"Geh, geh, geh..."
Hosoda's bulging belly pressed down on my stomach.
It felt like my guts were about to come flying out of my mouth.{p}

Blood gushed from my mouth like a fountain.
I saw Hosoda's face, drenched in that blood and dyed bright red.
Hosoda was grinning happily...{p}
